{"id":"resp_add46715c1ea07d1","created_at":1795610180,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_871674489bcf150d","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce final JSON with assessment, issues, questions, gap_review, coverage maybe optional. Must follow schema. Need to assess the SHACL candidate against requirement TRF-035 clause 4.1.1: \"L shall be taken as the ship's rule length used by the classification society.\"\n\nCandidate SHACL defines shape vocab:ShipRuleLengthShape targeting vocab:ship, requiring property vocab:ruleLength with node kind IRI (quantity value) and node shape that ensures qudt:numericValue decimal and qudt:unit unit:M.\n\nWe need to identify obligations and conditions from the represented source under approved scope. Obligation: The property L (rule length) must be present, numeric decimal, unit metre. Also L is the ship's rule length used by classification society. The requirement mentions L and also classificationSocietyRuleLength maybe? The source says L shall be taken as the ship's rule length used by classification society. So there is just one obligation: ensure ship has ruleLength value of type QuantityValue with numericValue decimal and unit metre. Possibly also need to ensure classificationSocietyRuleLength matches? But source doesn't require separate property; just description. However admission declares option A: recorded ruleLength and a separately supplied classificationSocietyRuleLength reference datum. The requirement may need both? But requirement only mentions L; extra property not needed. So shape includes ruleLength property correctly.\n\nNeed to check Input readiness: presence of property, node kind sh:IRI but should be sh:BlankNode or any? Actually ruleLength should point to QuantityValue node (a blank node with datatype). IRI is okay if quantity nodes are IRIs. Acceptable.\n\nCheck that they used sh:nodeKind sh:IRI - the shape expects the object to be IRI - but Requirement: \"value must be a qudt:QuantityValue\". Could be either IRI or blank node. IRI acceptable if individuals exist. So ok.\n\nPotential issue: sh:nodeKind sh:IRI but perhaps also need sh:class? They didn't enforce class qudt:QuantityValue. They only enforce node shape with properties numericValue and unit. That's fine.\n\nPotential missing: ensure unit is metre. They used sh:hasValue unit:M which is correct.\n\nPotential missing: ensure property is required (minCount 1) already.\n\nPotential missing: ensure that ruleLength is the ship's rule length used by classification society - may need to relate to classificationSocietyRuleLength via some relationship, but not required by clause. Could be optional.\n\nThus candidate implements obligation properly, so no defects.\n\nHowever need to check coverage for required injection: perhaps need to ensure that value is decimal, they have sh:datatype xsd:decimal yes.\n\nThus likely no issues; assessment APPROVE if all gap reviews are material false. Gaps: 5 gaps provided G1-5. They need gap_review entries with material false. In schema gap_review expects ids from G1..G5, material boolean, why string. Here we have none yet; we must fill.\n\nWe need to evaluate each gap. G1: missing source section 10 - that's a missing citation. That's material? Since the source has missing citation maybe not required for shape? Should be resolved? According to guidelines, missing source is not a code defect; it's a context gap, but if material (affects obligation) then need question. Probably not material for this shape. So we mark material false with why \"Citation missing but does not affect SHACL implementation of L requirement\". Similarly G2 section 3 missing, not material. G3 Table 3 multiple matches, not material. G4 Table 6, not material. G5 missing document UR P0, not material. Thus all gap_review material false.\n\nThus overall no issues, no questions.\n\nCoverage: we can optionally include coverage entries but not required. Schema expects coverage array optional. Could omit.\n\nThus produce JSON:\n\n{\n \"assessment\":\"APPROVE\",\n \"issues\":[],\n \"questions\":[],\n \"gap_review\":[\n   {\"id\":\"G1\",\"material\":false,\"why\":\"Citation missing but does not affect enforcement of ruleLength requirement\"},\n   {\"id\":\"G2\",\"material\":false,\"why\":\"Citation missing but not required for shape\"},\n   {\"id\":\"G3\",\"material\":false,\"why\":\"Multiple table matches irrelevant to ruleLength constraint\"},\n   {\"id\":\"G4\",\"material\":false,\"why\":\"Multiple table matches irrelevant\"},\n   {\"id\":\"G5\",\"material\":false,\"why\":\"Missing external document not needed for this SHACL\"}\n ]\n}\n\nMake sure order matches schema: gap_review array objects include id, material, why.\n\nNo coverage needed. Ensure fields exactly.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_9343f79cbe078f35","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"{\n  \"assessment\": \"APPROVE\",\n  \"issues\": [],\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"gap_review\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G1\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"Citation missing but does not affect enforcement of the ruleLength requirement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G2\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"Citation missing but is not required for the shape implementation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G3\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"Multiple table matches are unrelated to the ruleLength constraint\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G4\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"Multiple table matches are unrelated to the ruleLength constraint\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G5\",\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"why\": \"Missing external document does not impact the SHACL for ruleLength\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],